                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "### A.6 Non-Comparison to IProx",
            "block_bbox": [
                607,
                1217,
                914,
                1242
            ],
            "block_id": 18,
            "block_order": 13,
            "group_id": 18,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    607.0,
                    1217.0
                ],
                [
                    914.0,
                    1217.0
                ],
                [
                    914.0,
                    1242.0
                ],
                [
                    607.0,
                    1242.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Since IProX aligns gradients for its proxies on the full original gradient space of the model, whereas we use LoRA gradients, our methods are incompatible for comparison. We did indeed try some preliminary tests to see how well the two correlate, but unfortunately the influence spearman was very inconsistent depending on the run. Sometimes the LoRA gradients and IProX gradients tracked quite well, however any small change could cause the scores to plummet, and thus actionable results were difficult to reproduce.",
            "block_bbox": [
